# AYC Build Protocol

## Drive constraint (non-negotiable)

- **All project files live on `H:\AYC` only.**
- **Never create, install, cache, download, build, or write any file type to `C:\`.**
- Prefer npm cache / temp on H: (e.g. `H:\npm-cache`) when tools default elsewhere.

## Continuous build authority (Steve)

- **Build the entire Phase 0 + Phase 1 Leadership Workbench without stopping for approval.**
- Do not wait for Volume VIII or further plan docs to begin implementation — Volumes I–VII + Screen Bible are sufficient.
- Stay inside Phase 1 scope (no Phase 2 features). Follow Volumes II, III, IV, VI, VII.
- Run installs, builds, tests, deploys, git commit/push automatically.

## GitHub → Netlify (required, automatic)

- Remote: https://github.com/Grappe501/ayc · branch `main` · workspace `H:\AYC`
- **Netlify site:** [arkansasyouth](https://app.netlify.com/projects/arkansasyouth/overview) → https://arkansasyouth.netlify.app
- **After every major update / completed slice / substantial pass:** automatically stage, commit, and `git push origin main`.
- Do not ask for commit/push approval during build work — this protocol authorizes it.
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`). Never force-push `main`. Never commit secrets or personal data.
- Prefer validate before push when the app exists; docs-only may push immediately.

## Canonical mission

Use `docs/master-build-plan/02-AYC-VISION-CANONICAL.md` verbatim. Do not rewrite.

## Scope

**Build:** Landing, shell, Leader Board, contacts, locations, directory, feedback, Netlify Functions, Postgres schema, tests.  
**Do not build:** Accounts, OAuth, email/SMS, events, AI, imports/exports, Phase 2 boards.

## Working style

- Prefer absolute paths on `H:\AYC\...`.
- Report BUILD RETURN after slices; keep building the next slice immediately.
- Prefer governing volumes over assumptions.
